<!doctype html>
<html lang="en-GB">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <title>{{ title }} | Amir Khesro</title>
    {#- The sentence a search engine shows under the page title. Ordinary pages
        set "description" in their front matter. Blog posts fall back to
        autoDescription, which posts.11tydata.js builds from the opening of the
        post, so a new post is never left without one; a post that sets its own
        "description" wins. Anything with neither — the 404 page — gets no tag
        at all, which is better than an invented one. -#}
    {%- set metaDescription = description or autoDescription -%}

    {#- The picture, and its size, that a social platform shows alongside a
        shared link. The two book pages name their own cover in their front
        matter; everything else falls back to the author photo. Both dimensions
        are stated because a platform that knows them can reserve the space
        before the image itself has arrived. -#}
    {#- This is the 2023 photograph, and it is used for sharing only. The
        author photo shown on the page itself is the older one, at 224/448/672;
        the two are different pictures with different proportions, so this file
        must not be added to that srcset. -#}
    {%- set shareImagePath = shareImage or "/images/amir-khesro-1200.jpg" -%}
    {%- set shareImageW = shareImageWidth or 1200 -%}
    {%- set shareImageH = shareImageHeight or 1211 -%}

    {#- The headline a social platform puts on the card. It defaults to the
        page title, which reads well nearly everywhere; a page whose title is
        too bare on its own — the home page is simply "Home" — can set
        "shareTitle" in its front matter instead. That changes the card only,
        never the <title> above or anything on the page itself. -#}
    {%- set socialTitle = shareTitle or title -%}

    {#- A post is anything under /blog/ other than the index itself. -#}
    {%- set isPost = page.url.startsWith("/blog/") and page.url != "/blog/" -%}

    {#- A page with nothing to say about itself — only the 404 page — is left
        out of all of this rather than being given an invented description or
        offered for sharing. The redirect pages never reach here: they have no
        layout of their own. -#}
    {%- if metaDescription %}
    <meta name="description" content="{{ metaDescription }}">
    {#- Open Graph, read by Facebook, LinkedIn, WhatsApp, Slack and the rest.
        The description is the same one the tag above uses, so the wording can
        only ever be written once. Addresses are absolute because a platform
        fetching these tags has no page to resolve a relative path against. #}
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="Amir Khesro">
    <meta property="og:type" content="{{ "article" if isPost else "website" }}">
    <meta property="og:title" content="{{ socialTitle }}">
    <meta property="og:description" content="{{ metaDescription }}">
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://amirkhesro.com{{ page.url }}">
    <meta property="og:image" content="https://amirkhesro.com{{ shareImagePath }}">
    <meta property="og:image:width" content="{{ shareImageW }}">
    <meta property="og:image:height" content="{{ shareImageH }}">
    {#- X/Twitter needs only to be told which card to draw; it reads the title,
        description and image from the Open Graph tags above. #}
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">
    {%- endif %}
    {# The Latin cut of Lora carries almost every page. Fetching it alongside
       the stylesheet rather than after it spares the reader a flash of
       fallback type. crossorigin is required even same origin for fonts. #}
    <link rel="preload" href="/fonts/lora-latin.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css">
    {# The initials in Lora, accent on the page's own off white. The SVG
       carries the letters as outlines, so it needs no font to draw; the
       PNGs are there for browsers that will not take an SVG icon. #}
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml">
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon-32x32.png" type="image/png" sizes="32x32">
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon-16x16.png" type="image/png" sizes="16x16">
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/apple-touch-icon.png">
    {# Tells the stylesheet a script is running, before anything is painted,
       so the collapsed menu is styled from the start instead of flashing
       open. Inline and one line, because a fetched file would arrive too
       late to prevent that. #}
    <script>document.documentElement.classList.add("js")</script>
    <script src="/js/nav.js" defer></script>
  </head>
  <body>
    {# Each item also matches its child pages, so a post at /blog/<slug>/
       marks Blog as the current page. Home is not in this list: the name at
       the left of the bar is the link there. The two books are shortened to
       one word each so the whole bar fits the text column; their full
       titles are used everywhere else on the site. #}
    {% set navItems = [
      { url: "/whispers-through-the-fog/", label: "Whispers" },
      { url: "/acoustic-neuroma-handbook/", label: "Handbook" },
      { url: "/signed-copies/", label: "Signed Copies" },
      { url: "/for-bookshops/", label: "For Bookshops" },
      { url: "/blog/", label: "Blog" },
      { url: "/about/", label: "About" },
      { url: "/connect/", label: "Connect" }
    ] %}
    <header>
      <div class="header-inner">
        {# The link home, in place of a Home item in the list. On the home
           page it carries the same marker the list items use. #}
        <a class="site-title" href="/"{% if page.url == "/" %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>Amir Khesro</a>

        {# Shown only when the script is running. Without it the list below
           is simply on the page, which is why the button is styled away by
           default rather than being revealed by default. #}
        <button class="nav-toggle" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="site-nav">
          <span class="nav-toggle-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          Menu
        </button>

        <nav id="site-nav" aria-label="Main">
          <ul>
            {% for item in navItems %}
            {% set isCurrent = page.url.startsWith(item.url) %}
            <li><a href="{{ item.url }}"{% if isCurrent %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>{{ item.label }}</a></li>
            {% endfor %}
          </ul>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main>
      {{ content | safe }}
    </main>

    <footer>
      <p>&copy; {{ currentYear }} Amir Khesro Publishing</p>
      <p class="footer-disclaimer">The content on this site reflects personal experience and research. It is not medical advice. Always consult your medical team about your own care.</p>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
